#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# median

#% text
# `median(xs)` gives the middle value of the sorted list `xs`, or the mean of the two middle values when their number is even.

#% text
# `median(d)` gives the median of the distribution `d`, `quantile(d, 1/2)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The values of the list must be real numbers, so that they can be sorted.

#% item
# For a list of rows, the median is taken column by column.

#% item
# An empty list is an error.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The middle of three values:

#% cell
median([3, 1, 2])
#% output
#= 2

#% text
# An even number of values gives the mean of the two middle ones:

#% cell
median([4, 1, 3, 2])
#% output
#= 5/2

#% text
# The median of a distribution:

#% cell
median(exponential_distribution(2.0))
#% output
#= 0.34657359027997264

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Machine reals and fractions:

#% cell
[median([1.5, 9.0, 2.0, 2.5]), median([1, 1/2, 1/3])]
#% output
#= [2.25, 1/2]

#% text
# Column by column:

#% cell
median([[1, 5], [2, 4], [3, 9]])
#% output
#= [2, 5]

#% text
# Distributions with symbolic parameters:

#% cell
[median(normal_distribution(mu, sigma)), median(log_normal_distribution(m, s))]
#% output
#= [mu, exp(m)]

#% text
# A discrete distribution:

#% cell
median(poisson_distribution(3))
#% output
#= 3

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A typical value that one outlier does not move, unlike the mean:

#% cell
[median([1, 2, 3, 100]), mean([1, 2, 3, 100])]
#% output
#= [5/2, 53/2]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The median of a distribution is its quantile at 1/2:

#% cell
[median(exponential_distribution(l)), quantile(exponential_distribution(l), 1/2)]
#% output
#= [log(2)/l, log(2)/l]

#% text
# For a symmetric distribution, the median equals the mean:

#% cell
median(normal_distribution(3, 2)) == mean(normal_distribution(3, 2))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
median([quantity(1, "Meters"), quantity(3, "Meters"), quantity(150, "Centimeters")])
#% output
#= quantity(3/2, "Meters")

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Symbols cannot be sorted, so the median of a list of symbols stays unevaluated:

#% cell
median([a, b, c])
#% output
#= median([a, b, c])

#% text
# An empty list:

#% cell
median([])
#% output
#! failure(argument, median, "the list is empty")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `mean`, `quantile`, `sort`, `variance`, `std_dev`
